","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":9,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Downscale medical imaging to fit in GPU memory and the model loses the detail that catches faint findings.\n\n@epsilon_hq built its next-gen radiology AI models on a dedicated NVIDIA Blackwell Ultra cluster on Verda, now running 5x more experiments/week and training 3x faster. https://t.co/u2BB7ggxki","url":"https://x.com/verdacloud/status/2110673062140023006"},{"author_id":"2545814298","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:34:02.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110589994914263093"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/Prajhan_026/st…","end":304,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Prajhan_026/status/2109323427794616357","start":281,"url":"https://t.co/bM1am2sIE4"}]},"id":"2110589994914263093","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":85,"like_count":4,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":1},"text":"wait... two guys from coimbatore just trained an AI model from scratch on 4 GPUs in 76 hours??\n\nno research lab, no massive cluster....just 2 engineers\n\nfor context, here's what other teams spent training their models:\n-sarvam-1: ~122,880 gpu hours\nzoho zia 7b: ~153,600 gpu hours https://t.co/bM1am2sIE4","url":"https://x.com/adityafarrad/status/2110589994914263093"},{"author_id":"2070771579034996736","created_at":"2026-10-14T00:02:14.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110159207081091156"],"id":"2110159207081091156","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":10,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":1},"text":"Quote: University of Michigan CSE (Oct 12) — Software tools Perseus + Kareus can cut energy used to train large AI models by up to 40-50% without slowing training or hurting performance. Perseus slows GPUs that finish early and idle; Kareus optimizes task scheduling across the","url":"https://x.com/therealvane11/status/2110159207081091156"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110645408917549056"]},"author_id":"1053794036","created_at":"2026-10-15T08:14:35.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110645499782992254"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/MJqDHCONZ8","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Infernus_sl/status/2110645499782992254/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110645408917549056","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/MJqDHCONZ8"}]},"id":"2110645499782992254","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":50,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"🚨 Anthropic just warned that small AI models may be MONTHS away from copying themselves onto your smart devices.\n\nNot data centers. Smart ovens. Off-brand Android TV boxes.\n\nHere’s what the research actually says (and what it doesn’t) 🧵👇\n\nWhat happened\n\nOn Oct 12, Anthropic’s https://t.co/MJqDHCONZ8","url":"https://x.com/Infernus_sl/status/2110645499782992254"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110601937372524544"]},"author_id":"1648597885825556480","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:22:49.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110602274493857793"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/87oGaiOzYG","end":304,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/ConfiMind/status/2110602274493857793/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110601937372524544","start":281,"url":"https://t.co/87oGaiOzYG"}]},"id":"2110602274493857793","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":104,"like_count":5,"quote_count":1,"reply_count":2,"retweet_count":3},"text":"Introducing SampoTron: Our SOTA Cross-lingual Embedder\n \nCross-language retrieval is a real limitation in multilingual RAG: a Finnish query needs to surface an English passage, but most encoders don’t bridge that gap well. Fixing it usually means re-embedding your entire document https://t.co/87oGaiOzYG","url":"https://x.com/ConfiMind/status/2110602274493857793"},{"author_id":"1686364516534157313","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:54:23.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110353525981299004"],"id":"2110353525981299004","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":15,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"- GPU isn't always the problem. sometimes the real bottleneck is getting data to it. compute has been scaling faster than memory bandwidth and network performance in many workloads. buying a faster GPU doesnt automatically mean your training job gets proportionally faster.\n\n- a","url":"https://x.com/aniketmi_00/status/2110353525981299004"},{"author_id":"1665335769538392064","created_at":"2026-10-14T00:27:53.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110165660529573907"],"id":"2110165660529573907","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":87,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Your GPUs are sitting idle. Nvidia just open-sourced the fix.\nNvidia just gave away the software that decides who gets the GPUs.\n\nIt's called Run:ai. And it's now fully open source.\n\nSimple version:\n\nGPUs are the most expensive thing in AI. \n\nBut in most companies, they sit idle","url":"https://x.com/Ldataengineer/status/2110165660529573907"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2110384801282707457"]},"author_id":"1087750770148159490","created_at":"2026-10-14T14:58:42.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2110384810438832460"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":33,"id":"1554002744322584576","start":24,"username":"vcluster"},{"end":86,"id":"1265036057273384961","start":73,"username":"vclusterlabs"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/9sEs0g0bHy","end":299,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/saturn_cloud/status/2110384810438832460/photo/1","media_key":"3_2110384801282707457","start":276,"url":"https://t.co/9sEs0g0bHy"}]},"id":"2110384810438832460","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":54,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"📢 Saturn Cloud is now a @vcluster Stack. \n\nWe’re excited to partner with @vclusterlabs  to help AI clouds sell managed, per-token inference on their own GPUs.\n\nWith Stacks, op